cuems-engine (0.1.0rc6-6) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm:
    - 869fh8kef (#41): a project unload reaches the nodes as an unload. The
      controller used to forward it as a STOP, and a node's STOP re-arms the
      project it still holds, so every node killed its players and started
      new ones for a project that was no longer loaded, and kept its
      script, load status and /tmp/cuems.show.lock. The controller now
      removes its show lock and forwards /engine/command/unload; the node
      tears the project down as a load does (now shared as
      _teardown_project: cue threads, DMX blackout, video layers, mixer,
      audio players, disarm), aborts in-flight arms, forgets the script,
      sets load="", removes the lock and arms nothing. Refused while
      running. Ends the run for the cross-node follow relay like STOP and
      load.
    - Docs: the A/V loop sync guarantee (README, CLAUDE.md).
  * No dependency change (cuems-utils >= 0.1.0rc17). The whole cluster must
    run this engine: an older node has no unload handler and keeps the
    project armed until the next load.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:00:13 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc6-5) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm:
    - 869fhjdq5 (#35): stop_project ActionCue, the authored end of an
      unattended show. Every node reveals it and reports it to the
      controller, which runs its own STOP (running no, every cue 0, nodes
      re-armed); the first valid report wins, the others are dropped at
      INFO. The node never stops itself; a 3 s watchdog only logs. The cue
      is a hard chain break on the node; disabled, it is transparent
      (rehearsal mode). After the last cue the engine still keeps
      running=yes by design. Operator recipes in docs/unattended-playback.md.
    - Cue ADD/UPDATE reports are ignored while not running (a late start
      report after a STOP no longer leaves a cue at 1 or 100), and STOP
      restarts the arm watchdog ("Re-arm after STOP stalled").
    - 869fhjdp8: the dead script_finished aggregator is removed.
  * Depends on cuems-utils (>= 0.1.0rc17) for the schema value. The whole
    cluster must run this engine. Pairs with cuems-frontend PR #15 and
    cuems-power-bridge 0.3.1-2.

