cuems-engine (0.1.0rc6-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm; bump upstream version 0.1.0rc5 -> 0.1.0rc6.
  * GO anchor shipped by the controller (869f79ecc). Every node used to read
    its own MTC as the GO instant WHEN it executed the GO, so a node whose GO
    queued behind a slow command anchored its whole chain late. At Badajoz
    (0.1.0rc5-1), node02's first run after a cold boot played its video ~0.5 s
    behind: setnextcue's lookahead loaded three videos under the command lock
    and the GO that followed 0.2 ms later waited for it. The controller now
    captures the instant and ships it as {"go_mtc_ms": ...}; a node adopts it
    when its own lag is within [-200 ms, +10 s], logs "GO anchored at
    controller instant ...", and otherwise falls back to its local MTC with a
    WARNING. Mixed old/new controller and node versions keep working.
  * The controller only ships that anchor while its MTC is live
    (MtcListener.is_receiving(), any quarter frame or timecode sysex in the
    last 0.5 s). A dead MTC input used to become every node's anchor at 0.0,
    which fired the whole cluster seconds late; now it logs an ERROR and each
    node falls back to its own MTC.
  * setnextcue's lookahead runs on a PreArm:<cue> background thread, off the
    command lock, so the GO that follows a cue selection no longer waits for
    the next cues to load. Only the selected cue is still armed synchronously.
    The walk stops at its next cue on a new selection, a project reload or a
    STOP, and disarms what it armed if a different project was loaded
    meanwhile. Audio cues are pre-armed like any other local cue.
  * The arm-ahead walk treats other nodes' cues as transparent: no arm, no
    count toward its 2-cue budget, no lookahead depth consumed. In a mixed
    chain (node02 x3 -> node01 x3 -> controller x4) only the first node used to
    pre-arm its segment; the others re-armed at GO time on every run ("not
    loaded at go() time", late dispatches up to 840 ms on the controller).
  * The Auto continue chain is dispatched at its trigger, not cue by cue
    (869ej4x38): every cue's dispatch and run are scheduled from the trigger,
    each firing at trigger + its own prewait, so prewaits that run backwards
    fire on time instead of LATE (closes the gap 0.1.0rc5-1 only warned
    about). A chain epoch orders concurrent dispatches, a STOP takes the whole
    pending chain with it, and a cue enabled mid-chain rejoins at its own slot.
    A plain GO during an Auto follow tail still fires its target after the
    chain, as before (documented, not changed).
  * AudioMixer logs how long each JACK port took to register when it succeeds
    ("JACK port ... registered after Xs (attempt N/max)"), to size the 15 s
    registration ceiling from field data.
  * debian/rules builds the venv isolated from the build host
    (PIP_IGNORE_INSTALLED=1, PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1) and fails the build if
    python-rtmidi was not vendored. A host with python3-rtmidi installed made
    pip skip it, and the resulting deb left MTC reading 0.0 forever.
  * Depends: cuems-utils (>= 0.1.0rc13), was >= 0.1.0rc4. FadeActionHandler
    divides AudioCue.master_vol by 100, and only rc13 moved its default from
    1 (the old 0.0-1.0 scale) to 100: on an older cuems-utils a fade from an
    AudioCue with no deployed volume starts at 1%. The fleet already runs
    rc14; pyproject/poetry.lock require >= rc13 too (locked rc14).
  * CI installs librtmidi6 so the unit tests import cuemsengine again (they
    had silently run 0 tests on rc_1 since at least 2026-08-10); running them
    is what exposed the cuems-utils floor above. black/isort fixes on the
    files above.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:22:28 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc5-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm; bump upstream version 0.1.0rc4 -> 0.1.0rc5.
  * Auto continue now triggers the whole chain at one common trigger
    (869ej3cc8). CueHandler._chain_advance_ms returned prewait + postwait, so
    every cue's prewait cascaded into the arrival of every cue after it:
    prewaits authored as absolute offsets from GO (5/35/65/95/380 s) played as
    5/40/105/200/580, the last cue 3m20s late. Reported from Castillo Medina
    del Campo (cupula2, 0.1.0rc4-1) on an all-DMX project, where it reads as
    "auto follow" because each cue is on time relative to the previous one
    FIRING. The advance is now zero: every cue in the chain shares the trigger
    as its arrival and plays at trigger + its own prewait. postwait no longer
    gates a chain whose pointer has already advanced; it keeps its meaning as a
    real tail under Auto follow / Auto pause and as the cue's illumination hold.
    NOT a DMX-specific rule — the chain arithmetic never looks at cue type; DMX
    was simply the only type carrying a prewait in that show.
  * Chains whose prewaits run BACKWARDS are still reached after their own
    anchor and fire at dispatch; go_threaded now warns ("dispatched after its
    anchor — firing LATE by ..."), where it used to mistime silently. The
    dispatch reorder that closes the gap is deferred (see §8 of
    Plans/prewait-chain-trigger-semantics.md in cuems-RELATIONS).
  * ActionHandler planning docs and contracts landed on rc_1 since 0.1.0rc4-1;
    poetry.lock refreshed with the CI lint fix.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 14 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0200

cuems-engine (0.1.0rc4-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Merge rc_1 into debian/bookworm (source moved 52 files since 0.1.0rc3-1);
    bump upstream version 0.1.0rc1 -> 0.1.0rc4 to match.
  * PORT_HANDLER: make the port-exclusion list actually exclude (869ed9wf7).
    add_config_ports() passed set_ports() the same dict object it already
    held, so the `previous_ports == ports` guard was an identity check that
    always returned early and _all_used_ports stayed permanently empty — the
    engine could draw its own oscquery_ws_port (9190). Ports are now split
    into reservations (validated), config declarations (cannot raise) and
    system observations (cannot raise); the system scan is port-based via
    `ss -tuln` so it sees other users' sockets; draws reserve atomically and
    are bind-probed before being handed out. add_system_ports()/
    add_config_ports() moved to BaseEngine so the controller gets them too.
  * cuems-engine-mock: carry forward the no-op rsync shim and cuems-node-engine
    PATH drop-in introduced on rc_1 as 0.1.0rc2-3 (that entry is not in this
    changelog — it was added on the rc_1 line after 0.1.0rc3-1 forked).
    Retains the cuems-<component> wrapper names from 0.1.0rc3-2; the stale
    audioplayer-cuems/dmxplayer-cuems mock scripts are removed.

